  "details": "My partner recently had to switch to OSC-based eye tracking and there's a big issue where on her local end, her eye tracking looks smooth and fine. On the client end, AKA anyone else looking at her eyes, notices that the OSC-based eye tracking is very slow or jittery. I've included two videos, one of her POV, and one of me recording her on desktop(with about 70-80fps.) This must be an issue of some form and it would be nice if there could be a look into why this is happening. It was suggested by someone I know that it looks like there's no kind of interpolation, but I'm not sure if that is the issue. \nYoutube links to: \nHer video- https://youtu.be/jZ0c2T9Bfsk\nMy video- https://youtu.be/4e5ul-W9Y9Q\nAs you can tell, from her POV, everything seems smooth and nice. On my end, however, it seems slow and stuttery((especially on the eyelid/blinking side of things.) It is like this on all of her avatars that have eye tracking through OSC. I would happily send more videos if need be if it leads to fixing this.\nI'd really like to get this fixed so I could have my partner's eyes back properly and in good quality plss\n\nEdit: I've found a video by another creator showcasing the issue that explains it a bit better as well, and the issues it presents. It also presents a nearly unusable fix for it that requires more unnecessary avatar work and both radial menus being open at the same time(effectively negating it's usefulness as a concept for multiple reasons.)\nThe video: https://youtu.be/ueZVd4xEm-c",
